Aerie-Purpose: Seed Helium's AudioBuffer jitter from the site and session noise token and the sample coordinates only, so rendering the same audio graph again gives the same bytes and a tracker cannot average the noise away.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/audio_buffer.cc (AudioBuffer::JitterAudioData)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Amends helium-chromium/patches/helium/core/noise/audio.patch (issue #38). That patch xors
a process-wide base::AtomicSequenceNumber into the coordinate seed of every rendered
buffer, so each OfflineAudioContext render of the same graph on the same site got
different noise. Canvas noise is stable per site per session, which is the stronger design.
This patch drops the counter. The seed is now the channel (high bits) and the frame index,
mixed by BaseAudioContext::JitterAudioData with the per-site, per-session kAudio token and
the sample bits. The noise strength, the kHeliumNoiseAudio feature switch and the per-site
noise control (the token is absent when noise is off) are untouched.

Not changed: RealtimeAnalyser readbacks (getFloatFrequencyData and friends) still use their
own per-read counter. See the open question on issue #38.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/audio_buffer.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/audio_buffer.cc
@@ -30,7 +30,6 @@
 
 #include <memory>
 
-#include "base/atomic_sequence_num.h"
 #include "base/check_op.h"
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
 #include "base/containers/span.h"
@@ -57,14 +56,6 @@
 
 }  // namespace
 
-namespace {
-
-// Cheap per-render salt. This is not intended to be random; it just keeps
-// separate rendered buffers from sharing the same coordinate-noise stream.
-base::AtomicSequenceNumber g_helium_audio_render_sequence;
-
-}  // namespace
-
 AudioBuffer* AudioBuffer::Create(unsigned number_of_channels,
                                  uint32_t number_of_frames,
                                  float sample_rate) {
@@ -217,17 +208,18 @@
     return;
   }
 
-  const uint64_t render_seed =
-      static_cast<uint64_t>(g_helium_audio_render_sequence.GetNext());
   for (unsigned i = 0; i < channels_.size(); ++i) {
     if (NotShared<DOMFloat32Array> channel = getChannelData(i)) {
       base::span<float> samples = channel->AsSpan();
       for (size_t frame = 0; frame < samples.size(); ++frame) {
-        // Include render, channel, and frame coordinates so repeated equal
-        // sample values do not get identical coordinate jitter. The channel is
-        // shifted into high bits to avoid colliding with normal frame indices.
+        // Channel and frame coordinates only, so repeated equal sample values
+        // do not get identical coordinate jitter. There is no per-render
+        // salt: rendering the same graph again on the same site in the same
+        // session must give the same bytes, or a tracker can average the noise
+        // away. The channel is shifted into high bits to avoid colliding with
+        // normal frame indices.
         const uint64_t coordinate_seed =
-            render_seed ^ (static_cast<uint64_t>(i) << 48) ^ frame;
+            (static_cast<uint64_t>(i) << 48) ^ frame;
         samples[frame] = BaseAudioContext::JitterAudioData(
             samples[frame], context, coordinate_seed);
       }
